  "notes": "Subdivision-2 icosphere (42 vertices, 80 triangles) with a radial displacement of +-0.18 from five fixed sine terms of the unit direction, then scaled per axis to 0.0600 x 0.0550 x 0.0500 and lifted to z=0.  Subdivision 1 would be the bare 20-face icosahedron (12 vertices), which reads as a cut stone - that is why the level is 2.  Flat shading, so all 80 triangles stay hard facets.  Three slots by facet, all pure functions of the geometry: ink when n.z < -0.78 (the deepest underside folds, about 6 of the 80 facets), paper_dark when n.z < -0.50 or the fixed sine mask sin(37x+61y+89z) > 0.72, paper otherwise.  One shell, no texture.",
